@startuml
' The interesting path: a denial, and the auditor being woken by it.
title An unauthorised GET - denied, audited, and the watcher woken

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans

actor "kv_eve\n(uid 995, guest)" as Eve
participant "vaultctl" as CLI
box "kernel (ring 0)" #F4F4F4
  participant "kv_main\nioctl" as MAIN
  participant "kv_acl\nref. monitor" as ACL
  participant "kv_store" as ST
  participant "kv_audit\nring + wait queue" as AUD
end box
participant "AuditViewer\n(std::thread)" as AV
actor "kv_carol\n(uid 994, auditor)" as Carol

== before the attempt ==
Carol -> AV : start()
AV -> MAIN : open("/dev/kvault_audit")
note right of MAIN
  cursor starts at the current end of
  the log: the watcher streams what
  happens next, it does not replay
end note
AV -> AUD : poll(POLLIN)
AUD --> AV : blocks on the wait queue
note left of AV : no polling loop:\nthe thread sleeps until\nthe kernel wakes it

== the attempt ==
Eve -> CLI : vaultctl get db_password
CLI -> MAIN : ioctl(GET, "db_password")
MAIN -> MAIN : kv_check_name() ok
MAIN -> ST : kv_store_find()
ST --> MAIN : &secret
MAIN -> ACL : kv_acl_check(secret, uid 995, READ)
note right of ACL
  owner? no
  admin? no
  ACL: no entry for uid 995
       no entry for role guest
  role default for guest = 0
  ** denied **
end note
ACL --> MAIN : denied

MAIN -> AUD : log(995, GET, db_password, DENY, -EACCES)
activate AUD
AUD -> AUD : append under spinlock\n(safe: never sleeps)
AUD -> AV : wake_up_interruptible()
deactivate AUD

MAIN --> CLI : -EACCES
note right of MAIN
  Nothing was decrypted and nothing
  was copied back - not even a zeroed
  buffer. There is no path that returns
  a partial result.
end note
CLI --> Eve : "Permission denied"

== the denial is observed ==
AUD --> AV : POLLIN
AV -> AUD : read() one fixed-size record
AUD --> AV : {seq, ts, uid 995, pid, guest, GET,\n db_password, DENY, -13}
AV -> Carol : "uid=995 role=guest op=GET -> DENY"
note over Carol
  Eve cannot suppress this. The record
  is written by the same code path that
  refused her, before the error is
  returned to her.
end note
@enduml
